 character with modern luxury. Walls of glass frame the Pacific Ocean, flooding the interiors with natural light and creating the extraordinary sensation of floating above the sea, where sunrise coffees and sunset evenings become part of everyday life. Designed for both grand entertaining and intimate living, the home features four spacious bedrooms and five beautifully appointed baths. A stylish game room adds a relaxed social space, while a versatile garden room or creative studio offers endless flexibility. An additional large storage room can easily become a wine cellar, wellness retreat, gym or playroom. The three-car garage includes a generous work area, ideal for collectors, hobbyists, or those who value space and organization. It is also has plumbing in the lower level for a jacuzzi and or a cold plunge. Signature Palos Verdes stone, quarried directly from the property, is thoughtfully integrated throughout the home, grounding the architecture in a natural, organic elegance that is increasingly rare. Outdoors, a serene koi pond enhances the tranquil setting and can be converted into a custom pool if desired. This is more than a home, it is a private coastal sanctuary, a piece of architectural history, and a truly irreplaceable offering for the buyer seeking breathtaking views, architectural significance, and refined Southern California living. Please see the link for video.","Stone","Bonus Room, Center Hall, Family Room, Formal Entry, Game Room, Guest/Maid's Quarters, Kitchen, Laundry, Living Room, Main Floor Bedroom, Main Floor Primary Bedroom, Primary Bathroom, Primary Bedroom, Primary Suite, Office, Separate Family Room, Utility Room, Walk-In Closet, Workshop","","Palos Verdes Peninsula Unified","","","","","","","","","","","","","False","Full Service","Please text or call agent 24 hours before showing.","True","None","False","True","4992","Builder","","CA","Active","Two","","","Oceanaire","","43","Drive","","Mid Century Modern","Conventional","","24817"