d the San Gabriel Mountains across the private golf course, this home offers a daily backdrop that is truly exceptional. This beautifully appointed four-bedroom, four-and-a-half-bath home is enhanced by designer-selected finishes throughout, including custom lighting, window coverings, wallcoverings, hardware, and curated details that create a cohesive, sophisticated aesthetic. A private courtyard entry sets a welcoming tone and provides access to both the main residence, and the detached casita, which can be a guest suite with its own entrance, bathroom, and walk-in closet?ideal for guests, extended family, or a private office. Inside, stacked sliding glass doors open dramatically along two sides of the great room and the main-level primary suite, seamlessly blending indoor and outdoor living. High ceilings and rich hardwood floors connect the expansive great room to the gourmet kitchen, appointed with premium Wolf and Sub-Zero appliances. A walk-in wine pantry with a striking glass barn door adds both function and visual appeal. The dining room, great room, and primary suite are all positioned to capture the home?s stunning views. The primary suite features a luxurious bathroom with marble flooring, separate vanities, a soaking tub and a large shower, plus a walk-in closet with custom built-ins. In addition to the primary suite, a second bedroom suite inside the house on the main floor has its own bathroom and closet. Upstairs, a versatile bonus room, plus a sitting or study area and additional bedroom suite provide flexible living options. The resort-inspired backyard is designed for both relaxation and entertaining, featuring a sparkling pool and spa, fire pit, putting green, outdoor kitchen with bar and barbecue, and a large, covered dining patio?all set against a dramatic city lights backdrop.? This is a rare opportunity to own a refined yet relaxed home that delivers a true resort-style experience every day.","Spanish Tile, Tile","Bonus Room, Great Room, Kitc