ect Jack Ouzounian in 1963 and built as a piece of art by the original owner. The home is characterized by large open spaces that flow seamlessly into one another, this design utilizes smooth museum-quality plaster walls, hardwood and terrazzo floors and custom mahogany cabinetry to create a warm environment that is minimal and without excessive ornamentation. The detailing is simple but impeccable, for example, many of the doors are eight feet high and are crafted precisely so that they are void of trim and casings. Daylighting is a key feature. Large windows that extend to the ceiling flood the interior with natural light while emphasizing the connection to nature; and the expansive south-facing deck serves as an ""outdoor living room"" that wonderfully compliments the indoor environment. A truly special place to call home.","","Family Room, Great Room, Kitchen, Living Room, Main Floor Bedroom, Primary Bathroom, Primary Bedroom, Primary Suite","","Palos Verdes Peninsula Unified","","","","","Chris","Adlam","VADLACHR","V8107","","","Vista Sotheby's International Realty","2187500","False","Full Service","Call/text Kevin Moen To Show: 310 466-4656 Public Open House: Sat. 5/17 1pm-4pm Sun. 5/18 1pm -4pm","True","None","False","","2619","Assessor","","CA","Closed","Two","","","Via Boronada","","1737","","","Mid Century Modern","Cash, Cash to New Loan","","6889","","Single Family Residence","","Natural Gas Connected, Sewer Connected, Water Connected","Ocean, Panoramic, Trees/Woods","True","","","","1963","90274","1859","PVR1YY"
