nd everywhere. It's not unusual to stumble upon live music events at the historic Malaga Cove Library (they host amazing summer concerts) or to head down to RAT Beach for surfing, sunbathing, or just a stroll by the shore. When you walk into the house, you're greeted by an open floor plan with big windows showing off stunning ocean views. The gourmet kitchen has been totally revamped with a center island, shiny countertops, a custom backsplash, and high-end stainless steel appliances, it's the kind of place where everyone will want to hang out. Right off the kitchen is a spacious deck, perfect for barbecues or watching the sunset with friends. Head downstairs to find three large bedrooms, including two primary suites. One of them has a private deck that connects to its own living space imagine winding down there after a fun day at the beach or the golf club. And wait till you see the third level: a brand-new saltwater pool, spa, and pool deck (plus a pizza oven for when you're craving something delicious). There's also a fourth bedroom with its own living area and bathroom, which is super convenient for visitors or anyone who wants a little extra privacy. Everything in this home has been updated from bathrooms and decks to HVAC, landscaping, and moreso you can pretty much move in without any worries. And the location on Via Pinale is right in the heart of all that Malaga Cove has to offer tennis clubs, the Palos Verdes Golf Club, and a friendly community that makes you feel right at home. If you're looking for a place where you can enjoy the SoCal coast every day whether you're grabbing coffee in the plaza, catching a concert at the library, or just watching the waves roll in this is it. It's the kind of place you'll never want to leave! For more local happenings, check out Malaga Cove Concerts, Malaga Cove Library, and Malaga Cove Plaza. And don't forget to visit RAT Beach for your daily dose of surf and sun!","","Office, Walk-In Closet","","","","","","CLW-1001457