s kind to grace the MLS in some time, cherished by the same family since its construction 65 years ago. Step into a light-filled entry, featuring an adjacent en-suite bedroom perfect for guests, a nanny, or a private home office. A floating staircase leads to the expansive north-facing living room, bathed in natural light and anchored by a striking east-wall fireplace. The main level embodies the essence of mid-century design, showcasing newly refinished oak hardwood floors that glow with warmth, uncovered for the first time in decades. The tastefully remodeled kitchen flows seamlessly into a spacious dining room, where a south-facing glass wall frames serene views of a tranquil waterfall and pond, sure to be the backdrop for making wonderful memories no matter the season. Down a wide hallway, the private wing offers two generously sized bedrooms with vaulted ceilings, large closets, and west-facing windows that invite abundant light, separated by an open bathroom and laundry. The master suite, a true retreat, boasts soaring ceilings, ample closet space, a dressing area, and peaceful views of the lush, landscaped backyard. While nobody knows for sure, family lore claims famed architect A. Quincy Jones is responsible for the masterfully struck lines of this home - A timeless Southern California classic - Sure to take you back to the comfort of a gentler time. Set on manicured grounds, this home features a large driveway with extra off-street parking and an enviable Palos Verdes Estates location. With its unique orientation, elevation, and timeless style, this architectural treasure is a must-see. Don?t miss your chance to own your own piece of Valmonte!","Concrete","Kitchen, Laundry, Living Room, Main Floor Bedroom","","Palos Verdes Peninsula Unified","","","","","Daniel","Lowe","CLW-C103633","CLW-X81461","","","Compass","2100000","False","Full Service","Lockbox goes on Thursday morning. Afterwards - Go direct. Please remove shoes in doors or use booties provided.","